  "accent": "#7A2E5F",
  "accentDark": "#E080BF",
  "tiers": false,
  "notes": [
    [
      "Each part stands on the last but tells its own story.",
      "A new JoJo, a new era and a mostly new cast every time; earlier parts pay off later, but every part opens fresh, and a part boundary is a clean place to pause."
    ],
    [
      "Where each part sits in the overall numbering.",
      "Phantom Blood is episodes 1–9 and Battle Tendency 10–26 — one 2012 season split between them, so their rows keep that numbering; Stardust Crusaders runs 27–74, Diamond Is Unbreakable 75–113, Golden Wind 114–152, Stone Ocean 153–190 and Steel Ball Run from 191, each numbered from 1 as broadcast."
    ],
    [
      "Steel Ball Run is still airing.",
      "A new episode reaches Netflix each Friday. The 4 dated ones still to come carry the day they air, and are numbered rather than named until titles are published."
    ],
    [
      "The manga continues past the anime.",
      "It carries on with JoJolion and The JoJoLands, and has a list of its own."
    ],
    "Episode titles machine-read from the six Wikipedia season articles; every part's numbering is asserted complete, and Steel Ball Run's aired count checked against its article's own infobox, before this builds. Where a release renamed an episode to dodge a music trademark, the broadcast title stays."
  ],
